# systemd splits $EARLYOOM_ARGS on whitespace without removing quotes, so the
# --avoid regexp is left unquoted. The stock file quotes it, which makes earlyoom
# match literal quote characters and silently protect nothing.
#
# 8%/4% of 32 GiB is roughly 2.6 GiB before SIGTERM and 1.3 GiB before SIGKILL,
# and both the memory and the swap threshold have to be crossed before earlyoom
# acts. The avoid list keeps the session itself alive so a kill leaves a usable
# desktop instead of a black screen.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -m 8,4 -s 8,4 --avoid ^(systemd|Hyprland|kitty|waybar|sshd|dbus-.+|pipewire|pipewire-.+|wireplumber)$"
